# The nested directories are their own git repositories, with their own
# histories, remotes and release tags:
#
#   rpg-master/   github.com/colinhiggs/rpg-master
#   rules/ico/    github.com/colinhiggs/ico-adventures-rules
#
# They are ignored here on purpose. Adding a repository to a repository
# without making it a submodule records a bare commit hash and no way to
# fetch it, which looks fine locally and is unusable anywhere else.
#
# Making them submodules would be worse rather than better. This is the
# working directory the rules and the toolset are *written* in, and its
# copies are meant to move freely and often; a pin here would be a
# second thing to bump on every commit, recording nothing that the two
# repositories do not already record for themselves. The adventures
# project pins them because it consumes released versions. This one does
# not.
#
# So this repository tracks only what belongs to the working directory
# itself: the guidance and notes that span both projects.
/rpg-master/
/rules/

# Python bytecode, wherever it lands.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
